00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:10.660
Right.

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:28.220
Like if you put a character that controlled like Mario or Mega Man or, um, uh, Ninja Gaiden, it, you know, if you had a good controlling character, would it be fun to have them move around this side scrolling environment and collect these items?

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:38.400
I think the, the issue there is that it's still not just the fact that like, yeah, items are just kind of laid out and you just have to, you know, avoid pitfalls and enemies.

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:43.600
The issue there is the size of the rooms, which are all the same space.

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:45.240
It's just how they lay out the platforms.

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:48.940
There's really not for, for a momentum based character.

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:52.720
There's really not a lot of room to do any of that kind of stuff.

00:19:52.720 --> 00:20:07.440
Like in Prince of Persia, an example you used earlier, like that is a game that purposefully designs the, um, you know, the gaps and the floors and the traps to be based on how the character controls.

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:15.820
And in this game, I feel like most of the levels are designed without thinking about how Dash responds.

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:26.940
Like most things are just like, you know, like the trampolines, for instance, they just feel like something that you use because they couldn't figure out any other way for Dash to travel between these two areas.

00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:31.520
Exactly. So yeah, I think that's, that's a perfect way to articulate it.

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:44.300
The difference between this and Prince of Persia is that Prince of Persia, while it is, it is difficult at times, like it is designed to be, uh, to get you into a state of flow.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:53.580
Like if, if you're good at that game, you can kind of just, everything kind of feels second nature and you can, it feels fluid to go through these levels.

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:57.720
And in this game, it, it doesn't have that.

00:20:57.720 --> 00:21:11.240
Like every, every platform seems to be designed to slow you down unless it's explicitly like trying to get you to like go down a series of slides and then jump at the right moment.

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:13.100
Like those, those moments are few and far between.

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:18.940
And then to make up for that and how like, it is just hard to get around.

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:22.900
They just litter it with trampolines, which in and of themselves slow you down.

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:25.980
